# Real Device Testing

## ADB device is always connected
The owner keeps a physical Android device connected via ADB at all times. Agents **must** use it for verification.

## When to test on device
- After **any** mobile app change — UI, translations, logic, navigation, ads, permissions.
- After **any** backend change that affects what the mobile app displays (points, leaderboard, impact data, content).
- Before declaring any mobile feature "done" or "verified."

## How to test
1. Run `adb devices` to confirm device is connected.
2. Build and install: `flutter build apk --debug` then `adb install -r <path>`.
3. For release verification: `flutter build apk --release` then install and test — but see **AdMob invalid-traffic safety** below before touching any release build with live ads.
4. Use `adb logcat` to capture runtime errors during testing.
5. Take screenshots with `adb exec-out screencap -p > screenshot.png` for evidence.
6. Test in **at least 2 languages** — English plus one other (preferably Romanian as it has the longest labels).

## What to verify on device
- All screens render without overflow, truncation, or layout breaks.
- **Whole-frame UI audit every visit (stop 51 · 2026-08-09):** even if you opened the app to test something else, scan Channel, TODAY tiles, points labels, scroll cue overlap, marquee readability, i18n. Read-tool every screenshot.
- All strings are translated — no English leaking in non-English locale.
- Navigation works — no dead buttons, no stuck screens.
- Ads load where expected (app-open on launch, interstitial before quiz, banner on pages).
- Points display correctly after earning actions.
- Community posts/comments can be created and appear in feed.
- Legal pages load with correct content for the selected language.

## AdMob invalid-traffic safety (LOCKED 2026-07-26 — after a real 29-day suspension)
Agent ADB testing on a **release build with production ad units** generated ~€1.29 of
invalid ad traffic and got the AdMob/AdSense account (pub-8112542727970759) suspended
for 29 days (email 2026-07-24; reinstatement ~2026-08-22). This must NEVER repeat:

- **Default test build = debug APK.** Debug/profile builds use Google sample ad units
  (`lib/core/utility.dart`, `kReleaseMode` gate) — always safe for agents.
- **Never run agent test sessions on a release/Play build with production ad units.**
  If a release build must be verified, do it only after the device is registered as an
  AdMob test device (`NeoXten-Automation-Framework/scripts/plastypesa/ADMOB_TEST_DEVICE.md`),
  keep the session minimal, and never tap or click any ad.
- **Never tap, click, or auto-navigate through ads on production units** — not even once.
- During the suspension window follow
  `NeoXten-Automation-Framework/scripts/plastypesa/ADMOB_SUSPENSION_PAUSE.md`;
  `npm run test:plastypesa-ad-phase1` stays hard-blocked.
- If a release build is found installed on the ADB device when starting ad-touching work,
  flag it to the owner and install the debug APK before proceeding.

## Never
- Declare mobile work "done" without installing on the real device.
- Skip device testing because "it works in the emulator" or "the code looks correct."
- Ignore layout issues visible on device — if text is truncated or overlapping, it's a bug.
